@startuml dyn-provisioning
!include include/palette.puml

title Dynamic: phase-1 provisioning order, P1-01 to P1-13 (ADR-IR34 phase-1 plan, §11.9, docs/bootstrap.md)

<style>
activityDiagram {
  activity {
    BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor #555555
    MaximumWidth 340
  }
  arrow {
    LineColor #555555
  }
  note {
    MaximumWidth 300
  }
  .azure {
    BackgroundColor $C_AZURE
    FontColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_AZURE
  }
  .codefresh {
    BackgroundColor $C_CODEFRESH
    FontColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_CODEFRESH
  }
  .octopus {
    BackgroundColor $C_OCTOPUS
    FontColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_OCTOPUS
  }
  .argocd {
    BackgroundColor $C_ARGO
    FontColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_ARGO
  }
  .github {
    BackgroundColor $C_GITHUB
    FontColor #FFFFFF
    LineColor $C_GITHUB
  }
}
</style>

start
:**P1-01 Main loop**
Codefresh clean start: export, then delete the
old projects, contexts and integrations; keep
Git integration github-aisf-sample-apps; <<codefresh>>
:**P1-02 Provisioner** (operator session)
terraform/foundation: first apply on local state,
then foundation.tfstate migrates to
<tfstate-storage-account-global>; <<azure>>
note right
  Before the apply the provisioner creates
  group platform-operators with az.
  Creates groups, registry and scope maps,
  state and backup accounts, identities,
  every grant, budgets (skipped on offers
  that Cost Management does not support)
end note
fork
  :**P1-03 User as subscription Owner**
  Grant-ProvisionerRights.ps1 -SkipEntra:
  12 roles, ABAC condition replaced; <<azure>>
  note right
    Nothing waits for it. After P1-08 the
    main loop re-applies the foundation with
    conformance_least_privilege = true; then
    -ApplyLocks: CanNotDelete on
    rg-platform-global, rg-platform-build,
    rg-platform-prod-data
  end note
  detach
fork again
  :**P1-04 Provisioner**
  terraform/build: aks-platform-build
  (build.tfstate, global account); <<azure>>
  :**P1-04 Provisioner**
  Helm cf-runtime 10.5.6 in namespace codefresh,
  <cf-runtime> becomes the account default; <<codefresh>>
  :**P1-05 Main loop**
  Five ACR tokens and the conformance secret
  by CLI, then codefresh/register.sh --full; <<codefresh>>
fork again
  :**P1-06 Space Manager**
  octopus/terraform through octopus/apply.sh:
  moved blocks, accounts, feed acr-apps, pools,
  app project shells, ArgoCD.RepoReadCredential
  for env-apply (octopus-space.tfstate); <<octopus>>
  :**P1-06 Space Manager**
  First platform-wake release 0.0.1; <<octopus>>
  :**P1-07 Main loop**
  One pull request fills the placeholders
  of both tiers (tfvars, bootstrap, tenant); <<github>>
  :**P1-07 env-plan, env-apply in infra-nonprod**
  terraform/tier (tier-nonprod.tfstate): AKS,
  network, vault, apr-sleep-nonprod, Argo CD
  bootstrap, workers k8s-tdd and k8s-uat; <<octopus>>
  :**P1-07 Main loop**
  Ingress IP into the tenant values,
  octopus/apply.sh again (Platform.AppsDomain),
  seeds <kv-platform-nonprod> as platform-operators;
  :**P1-08 env-apply in infra-prod**
  terraform/tier (tier-prod.tfstate),
  then the same follow-ups for prod; <<octopus>>
  :**P1-09 apps-plan, apps-apply per app and tier**
  terraform/apps/tier (apps-<app>.tfstate):
  vaults and passwords, disks, backups, appi; <<octopus>>
  :**P1-09 Provisioner**
  terraform/apps/grants per app
  (app-grants-<app>.tfstate): deploy identities
  of workorders; sandbox tdd vault grant; <<azure>>
  :**P1-09 Space Manager**
  octopus/apply.sh again: real client IDs
  of the azure-<app>-<env> accounts; <<octopus>>
  :**P1-10 Argo CD argocd-<tier>**
  ApplicationSet apps renders tenant-<app>:
  databases, signer policies, backup CronJobs; <<argocd>>
end fork
:**P1-11 Main loop**
<sandbox-app-repo> from fixtures/sandbox-app/,
register.sh --app sandbox, the unsigned
fixture, the first sandbox release to prod; <<codefresh>>
:**P1-12 Main loop**
End-to-end pass on app #1: pull request against
master of 20260923-001, CI, release, tdd, uat, prod;
:**P1-13 Codefresh**
platform-env/conformance-arm, conformance and
conformance-destructive until green; then the crons; <<codefresh>>
stop

legend right
  |<$C_AZURE>    | Azure: Terraform as the provisioner, the Owner script |
  |<$C_CODEFRESH>    | Codefresh: runner, contexts, pipelines |
  |<$C_OCTOPUS>    | Octopus: octopus/terraform, releases, runbooks as id-platform-lifecycle-<tier> |
  |<$C_ARGO>    | Argo CD: applies what main holds |
  |<$C_GITHUB>    | GitHub: pull request to the environment repo |
  |<#FFFFFF>    | Operator steps across tools |
endlegend
@enduml
